@startuml llre-compilation
' Compilation pipeline for a `.llre` file (LibLevenshtein Regex Expression). The
' source text is lexed and parsed into an AST; named symbols imported from `.llev`
' files are inlined by the symbol expander; the NFA compiler lowers the expanded
' AST to an NFA (stored / serialised via compiled.rs). Because the construction is
' Thompson/Glushkov, matching is linear-time and ReDoS-resistant by construction.
' Colour mapping (per the canonical legend):
'   DSL compilation stages  brown  #D7CCC8 (container) / #EFEBE9 (child tint)
'   phonetic-engine output  pink   #F8BBD0
'   safety note            green   #C8E6C9
' Arrow colour = DSL border #4E342E for the compile flow.
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam rectangle {
  RoundCorner 14
  BorderColor #455A64
  FontColor #102027
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowThickness 2

left to right direction

title `.llre` regex compilation — source → lexer → parser → AST → symbol expander → NFA compiler → NFA

rectangle ".llre source" as SRC #D7CCC8
rectangle "lexer" as LEX #EFEBE9
rectangle "parser\n(src/phonetic/llre/parser.rs)" as PARSE #EFEBE9
rectangle "AST\n(ast.rs)" as AST #EFEBE9
rectangle "symbol expander\n(symbol_expander.rs)" as EXPAND #EFEBE9
rectangle "NFA compiler\n(nfa_compiler.rs)" as NFAC #D7CCC8
rectangle "NFA\n(compiled.rs)" as NFA #F8BBD0

SRC    -[#4E342E]-> LEX
LEX    -[#4E342E]-> PARSE
PARSE  -[#4E342E]-> AST
AST    -[#4E342E]-> EXPAND
EXPAND -[#4E342E]-> NFAC
NFAC   -[#AD1457]-> NFA

note bottom of NFAC #C8E6C9
  Thompson/Glushkov construction ⇒
  linear-time matching, ReDoS-resistant
  by construction.
end note
@enduml
